    "title": "Caitlin Clark live score updates, stats, highlights today for USA Basketball vs. Spain",
    "text": "Updated March 17, 2026, 6:57 p.m. ETThe 24-year-old Caitlin Clark averaged 11.6 points and 6.4 assists in the Americans' five wins.Indiana Fever star Caitlin Clark has 7 points and 7 assists as USA Basketball finishes the FIBA World Cup qualifying tournament with an 84-70 win over Spain. The 24-year-old averages 11.6 points and 6.4 assists as the Americans goes 5-0. Kahleah Copper leads Team USA with 20 points and Kelsey Plum adds 18.The U.S. has already qualified for the World Cup, set for September in Berlin, Germany, but it competed to get extra reps for younger players on the national team. Caitlin Clark stats, points, assists today for USA Basketball vs. Spain in World Cup qualifyingUSA 61, Spain 47, end 3Q: Caitlin Clark assists Kahleah Copper and Paige Buckers on 3-pointers. She also steals a pass and scores.USA 44, Spain 32, halftime: Kelsey Plum leads Team USA with 10 points.USA 31, Spain 23, 5:47 left 2Q: Caitlin Clark has 5 points and 4 assists as she returns to the bench, but not before she delivers this long pass to Paige Bueckers.USA 21, Spain 16, end 1Q: Caitlin Clark makes a 3-pointer and 2 free throws, and she has 2 assists. Megan Gufstason, a University of Iowa player before Clark's time, scores 7 early points for Spain. Clark enters the game at the 6:24 mark as the USA leads 8-5.Where to watch Caitlin Clark, USA Basketball vs. Spain tomorrow, Tuesday, March 17, 2026USA holds a 10-0 record over Spain, with the countries last playing in 2016. USA Basketball will tip off against Spain at 5 p.m. ET Tuesday, March 17, to finish the qualifying tournament.Watch Caitlin Clark, USA Basketball on Sling!Does Caitlin Clark play today? Caitlin Clark plays in USA vs Spain women's basketball game tonight Tuesday, March 17, 2026Caitlin Clark and USA Basketball play Game 5 against Spain at 5 p.m. ET Tuesday, March 17.Buy Caitlin Clark gear on Fanatics!What time does Caitlin Clark play today? When does USA Basketball play Spain in FIBA World Cup qualifier tonight, Tuesday, March 17, 2026?Caitlin Clark and USA Basketball return to action today against Spain at 5 p.m. ET Tuesday, March 17.Where is USA Basketball, Caitlin Clark playing in the 2026 FIBA World Cup qualifiers?The tournament is being hosted in San Juan, Puerto Rico.When is Caitlin Clark's next game? When is the next USA Basketball game in 2026 FIBA World Cup qualifiers?The group stage finale, the fifth game of the trip, may be the most competitive for the U.S. They will play Spain at 5 p.m. ET Tuesday, March 17.Buy Caitlin Clark's Nike merch!Caitlin Clark points, stats, in USA Basketball games at 2026 FIBA World Cup qualifiersIn 19 minutes, Caitlin Clark scored 17 points with 12 assists to two turnovers in a tournament-opening 110-46 win over Senegal on Wednesday. Read more here.Clark's offense was not as effective in her second game, that in as many days after eight months recovering from an injury. She finished with eight points, three rebounds and two assists in the 91-48 win over Puerto Rico on Thursday. Read more here.Clark then looked better in her third game, a 93-59 win over Italy, finishing with 12 points on 4-of-5 shooting with five assists and a steal. There was better flow within the offense, and she even had a steal and a transition bounce pass that threaded the needle for a layup.In the fourth game of the tournament, Clark got her first start with the senior national team. She had 14 points on 6 of 11 shooting (2 of 7 on 3s), a team-high six assists and two steals.USA Basketball results at 2026 FIBA World Cup qualifying tournamentWednesday, March 11: USA 110, Senegal 46. INSIDERThursday, March 12: USA 91, Puerto Rico 48. INSIDERSaturday, March 14: USA 93, Italy 59. INSIDERSunday, March 15: USA 101, New Zealand 46. INSIDERUSA Basketball schedule in 2026 FIBA World Cup qualifying tournamentTuesday, March 17: vs Spain, 5 p.m. ET, TruTV, HBOWatch Caitlin Clark, USA Basketball live!Chloe Peterson is the Indiana Fever beat reporter for IndyStar. Reach her at capeterson@gannett.com or follow her on X at @chloepeterson67.Get IndyStar's Indiana Fever and Caitlin Clark coverage sent directly to your inbox with our Caitlin Clark Fever newsletter. Subscribe to IndyStar's YouTube channel for Fever Insiders Live.",
